completed_at: "2026-08-01T05:28:00.591Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: "Chain-invariant envelope metadata is emitted once per cursor chain and referenced on continuation pages, or is suppressible by an explicit caller opt-out, and the reduction is measured; Page size is derived from the measured bytes-per-row of the projection against the remaining budget rather than from a fixed constant, so a larger budget yields more rows rather than the same two; A gate asserts that walking a full result set through any bounded intent costs no more total tokens than the unprojected single call for the same set, on a corpus at least the size of the current tracker; The published evidence table records bytes per row and total walk cost for every bounded read family member before and after, including the 315-item list case; A negative control proves the gate fails when per-page metadata is reintroduced on every page"
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: Cursor continuations reference invariant metadata and preserve every ordered row with fail-closed stable identity
expected_result: Budgeted list and search cursors walk every ordered result exactly once while using materially fewer bytes than repeated unbounded retrieval.
actual_result: "List/search walk 1,998 rows without duplication, omission, or reorder at 0.2208 and 0.2391 of unbounded byte cost"
